# Production environment variables.
#
# The core experience requires NONE of these. Local development, `npm test` and
# `npm run build` all run with zero configuration: with no DATABASE_URL the app
# uses an embedded PGlite database, and no upstream feed needs a key.
#
# Only set these for a real deployment.

# Hosted Postgres connection string.
#
# In production khata refuses to start without this rather than silently using
# an embedded database, which would lose every saved ledger line on the next
# cold start. Locally, leaving it unset selects PGlite.
#
# Neon, Vercel Postgres, Supabase and any other Postgres all work.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# Postgres schema to place khata tables in. Defaults to "public".
# Set this when one Postgres instance is shared with another application.
# Must be a plain lowercase identifier.
# DATABASE_SCHEMA="khata"

# Canonical origin, used for metadata, OpenGraph, the sitemap and public/mcp.json.
# Set this to the real production alias after the first deploy so preview
# deployments do not advertise it.
# SITE_URL="https://khata-dqj3kgz0n-aniruddha-adaks-projects.vercel.app"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is deliberately no LLM_API_KEY variable.
#
# khata's open-weight model runs in the visitor's own browser via
# @huggingface/transformers, or against a local Ollama at 127.0.0.1:11434.
# No key is needed, nothing is billed, and the text of a household's messages
# is never sent to anyone we do not control. Do not add one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------